cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Pre-release draft. Not admitted, not peer reviewed. Cite only with this status."
type: article
title: "Planar Steiner diversities need logarithmic L1 distortion"
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeff
version: 0.0.0-draft
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - diversities
  - graph Steiner diversity
  - diamond graphs
  - treewidth
  - flow-cut gap
abstract: >-
  Unit diamond graphs are planar and have treewidth two, but their graph
  Steiner diversities require logarithmic L1 distortion. A generation-set
  cut certificate proves the explicit lower bound (6d+7+2/4^d)/9 after d
  replacement rounds. The same demands satisfy every cut condition but
  require at least this much fractional Steiner-tree routing congestion.
  A cited upper bound identifies the logarithmic order. Exact distortion
  beyond depth two is not determined here. Novelty remains unresolved.
